[[File:Starwalker (Beta 31.0).png|thumb|222x222px|Beta 31.0]]
Starwalker was added in '''Beta 30.0'''. Its first change, alongside many other Deltarune cards, was in '''Beta 31.0'''. It was buffed by triggering its effect if you have at least 2 spells in your hand instead of 3. This was reverted in '''Beta 35.0'''.
[[File:Starwalker (Beta 35.0).png|thumb|226x226px|Beta 35.0]]
'''Beta 52.1''' nerfed it further. Now if its effect triggers, its own cost is reduced by 2G instead of 3G. Since it's a 4G monster, this leaves it at 2G instead of 1G.
[[File:Starwalker (Beta 52.1).png|thumb|221x221px|Beta 52.1]]
'''Beta 53.0''' reworked it entirely, taking Ranger Rudinn's design by turning from a 3/2 [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Rare Rare] to a 4/4 [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Common Common] with the Magic of choosing a card in your hand and returning it to your deck with -4 cost. But this will only work if your hand lacks any Rare and [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Epic Epic] cards, just like [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Starwalker_Bird Starwalker Bird]. Luckily, during the transition, that effect was buffed to make generated cards (cards not starting in your deck) not be included.

